  "findings": [
    "Both requested DX12 cases fail compiling the cull compute pipeline in FXC (X3663 varying-control-flow thread synchronization and uninitialized instance_policy). There are no DX12 frame-time measurements.",
    "Four-view 4K default: CPU-submit 2.59/6.38 ms, serialized wall 7.57/12.85 ms, GPU 4.15/4.77 ms (median/p95). A median below 8.33 ms does not prove sustained 120 FPS or presented performance.",
    "One-view 1080p default: CPU-submit 0.79/2.53 ms, serialized wall 2.39/5.52 ms, GPU 1.18/1.50 ms.",
    "Renderer submit is the largest measured renderer CPU span; shade is the largest GPU pass in all successful runs. The CPU span does not isolate driver work from queue blocking.",
    "Sky tiles off slightly lowers GPU median (4.15 to 4.00 ms at 4K; 1.18 to 1.14 ms at 1080p), but wall medians are effectively unchanged/mixed. One ordered pass cannot establish a stable improvement.",
    "Tiled post off raises tonemap mean (0.176 to 0.303 ms at 4K, 0.043 to 0.073 ms at 1080p); whole-frame differences remain exploratory.",
    "Instance broadphase leaves GPU medians essentially unchanged and has a worse 1080p CPU-submit/wall tail in this pass (wall p95 11.66 vs 5.52 ms). Instance groups shows no clear overall win. Do not change defaults on these data alone.",
    "Startup renderer time varies substantially, including 4104 ms for 4K sky-tiles-off versus 83 ms default. Treat startup/cache behavior separately from the measured frame percentiles.",
    "This is a populated default bot fixture with full scene/FX uploads, not the separate sustained bullet/explosion stress fixtures or a Godot-matched workload. No cross-engine ratio."
  ],
